==================================================
January 30 is the 30th day of the year in the  [LINK: (Gregorian calendar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorian_calendar] ;  335 days remain until the end of the year (336 in  [LINK: (leap years) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leap_year] ).


# EVENTS #

[LINK: (1018) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1018]  –  [LINK: (Poland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poland]  and the  [LINK: (Holy Roman Empire) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Roman_Empire]  conclude the  [LINK: (Peace of Bautzen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_of_Bautzen] . [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-1]

[LINK: (1287) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1287]  – King  [LINK: (Wareru) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wareru]  founds the  [LINK: (Hanthawaddy kingdom) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanthawaddy_kingdom] , and proclaims independence from the  [LINK: (Pagan Kingdom) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pagan_Kingdom] . [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-2]

[LINK: (1607) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1607]  – An estimated 200 square miles (51,800 ha) along the coasts of the  [LINK: (Bristol Channel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bristol_Channel]  and  [LINK: (Severn Estuary) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Severn_Estuary]  in England are destroyed by  [LINK: (massive flooding) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1607_Bristol_Channel_floods] , resulting in an estimated 2,000 deaths. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-3]

[LINK: (1648) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1648]  –  [LINK: (Eighty Years' War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eighty_Years%27_War] : The  [LINK: (Treaty of Münster and Osnabrück) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_of_M%C3%BCnster]  is signed, ending the conflict between the Netherlands and Spain. [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-4]

[LINK: (1649) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1649]  –  [LINK: (Charles I of England) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_I_of_England]  is  [LINK: (executed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Execution_of_Charles_I]  in Whitehall, London. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-CharlesI-5]

[LINK: (1661) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1661]  –  [LINK: (Oliver Cromwell) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oliver_Cromwell] ,  [LINK: (Lord Protector) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_Protector#Cromwellian_republican_Commonwealth]  of the  [LINK: (Commonwealth of England) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonwealth_of_England] , is  [LINK: (ritually executed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Posthumous_execution]  more than two years after his death, on the 12th anniversary of the execution of  [LINK: (the monarch) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_I_of_England]  he himself deposed. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-6]

[LINK: (1667) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1667]  –  [LINK: (The Truce of Andrusovo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truce_of_Andrusovo]  is signed, ending the  [LINK: (Russian-Polish War of 1654-1667) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Polish_War_(1654%E2%80%931667)] . [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-7]  [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-8]

[LINK: (1789) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1789]  –  [LINK: (Tây Sơn) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%A2y_S%C6%A1n_dynasty]  forces  [LINK: (emerge victorious) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Ng%E1%BB%8Dc_H%E1%BB%93i-%C4%90%E1%BB%91ng_%C4%90a]  against  [LINK: (Qing) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qing_dynasty]  armies and liberate the capital  [LINK: (Thăng Long) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Th%C4%83ng_Long] .

[LINK: (1806) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1806]  – The original  [LINK: (Lower Trenton Bridge) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lower_Trenton_Bridge]  (also called the Trenton Makes the World Takes Bridge), which spans the  [LINK: (Delaware River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delaware_River]  between  [LINK: (Morrisville, Pennsylvania) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morrisville,_Bucks_County,_Pennsylvania]  and  [LINK: (Trenton, New Jersey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trenton,_New_Jersey] , is opened.

[LINK: (1820) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1820]  –  [LINK: (Edward Bransfield) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Bransfield]  sights the  [LINK: (Trinity Peninsula) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinity_Peninsula]  and claims the discovery of  [LINK: (Antarctica) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antarctica] .

[LINK: (1826) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1826]  – The  [LINK: (Menai Suspension Bridge) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Menai_Suspension_Bridge] , considered the world's first modern suspension bridge, connecting the  [LINK: (Isle of Anglesey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isle_of_Anglesey]  to the northwest coast of Wales, is opened.

[LINK: (1835) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1835]  – In the first assassination attempt against a President of the United States,  [LINK: (Richard Lawrence) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Lawrence_(failed_assassin)]  attempts to shoot president  [LINK: (Andrew Jackson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Jackson] , but fails and is subdued by a crowd, including several congressmen as well as Jackson himself.

[LINK: (1847) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1847]  –  [LINK: (Yerba Buena, California) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yerba_Buena,_California]  is renamed  [LINK: (San Francisco, California) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco,_California] . [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-9]

[LINK: (1858) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1858]  – The first Hallé concert is given in  [LINK: (Manchester) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manchester] , England, marking the official founding of  [LINK: (The Hallé) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hall%C3%A9]  orchestra as a full-time, professional orchestra.

[LINK: (1862) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1862]  –  [LINK: (American Civil War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Civil_War] : The first American  [LINK: (ironclad warship) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ironclad_warship] , the  [LINK: (USS Monitor) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USS_Monitor]  is launched. [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-10]

[LINK: (1889) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1889]  –  [LINK: (Archduke) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archduke]   [LINK: (Crown Prince Rudolf of Austria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crown_Prince_Rudolf_of_Austria] , heir to the  [LINK: (Austro-Hungarian) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austria-Hungary]  crown, is found dead with his mistress  [LINK: (Baroness Mary Vetsera) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baroness_Mary_Vetsera]  in the  [LINK: (Mayerling) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayerling_Incident] . [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-11]  [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-12]

[LINK: (1902) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1902]  – The first  [LINK: (Anglo-Japanese Alliance) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglo-Japanese_Alliance]  is signed in  [LINK: (London) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London] .

[LINK: (1908) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1908]  – Indian pacifist and leader  [LINK: (Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahatma_Gandhi]  is released from prison by  [LINK: (Jan C. Smuts) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_C._Smuts]  after being tried and sentenced to two months in jail earlier in the month.

[LINK: (1911) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1911]  – The destroyer  [LINK: (USS Terry) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USS_Terry_(DD-25)]  makes the first  [LINK: (airplane) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Airplane]  rescue at sea saving the life of  [LINK: (Douglas McCurdy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Alexander_Douglas_McCurdy]  16 kilometres (10 miles) from  [LINK: (Havana, Cuba) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Havana,_Cuba] .

[LINK: (1920) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1920]  – Japanese carmaker  [LINK: (Mazda) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mazda]  is founded, initially as a  [LINK: (cork) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cork_(plug)] -producing company. [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-13]

[LINK: (1925) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1925]  – The Government of  [LINK: (Turkey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkey]  expels  [LINK: (Patriarch Constantine VI) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantine_VI_of_Constantinople]  from  [LINK: (Istanbul) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Istanbul] .

[LINK: (1930) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1930]  – The  [LINK: (Politburo of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Politburo_of_the_Communist_Party_of_the_Soviet_Union]  orders the confiscation of lands belonging to the Kulaks in a campaign of  [LINK: (Dekulakization) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dekulakization] , resulting in the executions and forced deportations of millions. [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-14]

[LINK: (1933) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1933]  –  [LINK: (Adolf Hitler's rise to power) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolf_Hitler%27s_rise_to_power] : Hitler takes office as the Chancellor of Germany.

[LINK: (1939) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1939]  – During a  [LINK: (speech) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/30_January_1939_Reichstag_speech]  in the  [LINK: (Reichstag) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reichstag_(Nazi_Germany)] ,  [LINK: (Adolf Hitler) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolf_Hitler]  makes a  [LINK: (prediction) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hitler%27s_prophecy]  about the end of the  [LINK: (Jewish race) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jews]  in Europe if another  [LINK: (world war) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_war]  were to occur. [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-15]

[LINK: (1942) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1942]  –  [LINK: (World War II) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_II] : Japanese forces  [LINK: (invade the island of Ambon) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Ambon]  in the  [LINK: (Dutch East Indies) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dutch_East_Indies] . Some 300 captured Allied troops are killed after the surrender. One-quarter of the remaining POWs remain alive at the end of the war.

[LINK: (1944) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1944]  – World War II: The  [LINK: (Battle of Cisterna) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Cisterna] , part of  [LINK: (Operation Shingle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Shingle] , begins in central Italy.

[LINK: (1945) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1945]  – World War II: The  [LINK: (Wilhelm Gustloff) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KdF_Ship_Wilhelm_Gustloff] , overfilled with German  [LINK: (refugees) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refugee] , sinks in the  [LINK: (Baltic Sea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baltic_Sea]  after being  [LINK: (torpedoed) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torpedo]  by a  [LINK: (Soviet) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soviet_Union]   [LINK: (submarine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soviet_submarine_S-13] , killing approximately 9,500 people.

1945   – World War II:  [LINK: (Raid at Cabanatuan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raid_at_Cabanatuan] : One hundred and twenty-six American Rangers and Filipino resistance fighters liberate over 500 Allied prisoners from the Japanese-controlled Cabanatuan POW camp. [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-16]

[LINK: (1948) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1948]  –  [LINK: (British South American Airways) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_South_American_Airways] '  [LINK: (Tudor IV Star Tiger disappears) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BSAA_Star_Tiger_disappearance]  over the  [LINK: (Bermuda Triangle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bermuda_Triangle] .

1948   – Following the  [LINK: (assassination of Mahatma Gandhi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination_of_Mahatma_Gandhi]  in his home compound,  [LINK: (India) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India] 's prime minister,  [LINK: (Jawaharlal Nehru) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jawaharlal_Nehru] , broadcasts to the nation, saying " [LINK: (The light has gone out of our lives) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_light_has_gone_out_of_our_lives] ". [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-17]  [LINK: ([18]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-18]  The date of the assassination becomes observed as " [LINK: (Martyrs' Day) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martyrs%27_Day_(India)] " in India.

[LINK: (1956) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1956]  – In the United States,  [LINK: (Civil Rights Movement) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_Rights_Movement]  leader  [LINK: (Martin Luther King Jr.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Luther_King_Jr.] 's home is bombed in retaliation for the  [LINK: (Montgomery bus boycott) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montgomery_bus_boycott] .

[LINK: (1959) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1959]  – The forces of the Sultanate of Muscat occupy the last strongholds of the Imamate of Oman,  [LINK: (Saiq) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saiq]  and Shuraijah, marking the end of  [LINK: (Jebel Akhdar War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jebel_Akhdar_War]  in  [LINK: (Oman) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oman] . [LINK: ([19]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-OmansInsurgencies-19]

[LINK: (1959) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1959]  –  [LINK: (MS Hans Hedtoft) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MS_Hans_Hedtoft] , specifically designed to operate in icebound seas, strikes an iceberg on her maiden voyage and sinks, killing all 95 aboard.

[LINK: (1960) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1960]  – The  [LINK: (African National Party) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_National_Party]  is founded in  [LINK: (Chad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chad] , through the merger of traditionalist parties.

[LINK: (1964) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1964]  – In a bloodless coup, General  [LINK: (Nguyễn Khánh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nguy%E1%BB%85n_Kh%C3%A1nh]   [LINK: (overthrows) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_1964_South_Vietnamese_coup]  General  [LINK: (Dương Văn Minh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C6%B0%C6%A1ng_V%C4%83n_Minh] 's military junta in  [LINK: (South Vietnam) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Vietnam] .

[LINK: (1968) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1968]  –  [LINK: (Vietnam War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam_War] :  [LINK: (Tet Offensive) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tet_Offensive]  launch by forces of the  [LINK: (Viet Cong) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viet_Cong]  and  [LINK: (North Vietnamese Army) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People%27s_Army_of_Vietnam]  against South Vietnam, the United States, and their allies. [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-Chase2022-20]

[LINK: (1969) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1969]  –  [LINK: (The Beatles) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles] ' last public performance, on the roof of  [LINK: (Apple Records) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Records]  in London. The  [LINK: (impromptu concert) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beatles%27_rooftop_concert]  is broken up by the police. [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-Chase2022-20]

[LINK: (1972) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1972]  –  [LINK: (The Troubles) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Troubles] :  [LINK: (Bloody Sunday) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloody_Sunday_(1972)] :  [LINK: (British paratroopers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parachute_Regiment_(United_Kingdom)]  open fire on anti-internment marchers in  [LINK: (Derry) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derry] , Northern Ireland, killing 13 people; another person later dies of injuries sustained. [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-21]

1972   –  [LINK: (Pakistan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pakistan]  leaves the  [LINK: (Commonwealth of Nations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonwealth_of_Nations]  in protest of its recognition of breakaway  [LINK: (Bangladesh) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bangladesh] .

[LINK: (1974) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1974]  –  [LINK: (Pan Am Flight 806) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pan_Am_Flight_806]  crashes near  [LINK: (Pago Pago International Airport) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pago_Pago_International_Airport]  in  [LINK: (American Samoa) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Samoa] , killing 97. [LINK: ([22]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-22]

[LINK: (1975) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1975]  – The  [LINK: (Monitor National Marine Sanctuary) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monitor_National_Marine_Sanctuary]  is established as the first  [LINK: (United States National Marine Sanctuary) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_National_Marine_Sanctuary] .

1975   –  [LINK: (Turkish Airlines Flight 345) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkish_Airlines_Flight_345]  crashes into the  [LINK: (Sea of Marmara) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_of_Marmara]  near  [LINK: (Istanbul Yeşilköy Airport) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atat%C3%BCrk_Airport] , killing 42. [LINK: ([23]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-asn-23]

[LINK: (1979) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1979]  – A  [LINK: (Varig) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Varig]   [LINK: (Boeing 707-323C) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boeing_707-323C]  freighter, flown by the same commander as  [LINK: (Flight 820) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Varig_Flight_820] ,  [LINK: (disappears over the Pacific Ocean) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Varig_Flight_967]  30 minutes after taking off from Tokyo.

[LINK: (1982) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1982]  –  [LINK: (Richard Skrenta) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Skrenta]  writes the first PC  [LINK: (virus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_virus]  code, which is 400 lines long and disguised as an  [LINK: (Apple) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Computer]  boot program called " [LINK: (Elk Cloner) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elk_Cloner] ".

[LINK: (1989) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1989]  – The American  [LINK: (embassy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embassy_of_the_United_States,_Kabul]  in  [LINK: (Kabul) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kabul] ,  [LINK: (Afghanistan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Republic_of_Afghanistan]  is closed.

[LINK: (1995) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1995]  –  [LINK: (Hydroxycarbamide) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydroxycarbamide]  becomes the first approved preventive treatment for  [LINK: (sickle cell disease) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sickle_cell_disease] .

[LINK: (2000) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000]  –  [LINK: (Kenya Airways Flight 431) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenya_Airways_Flight_431]  crashes into the Atlantic Ocean off the coast of  [LINK: (Ivory Coast) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivory_Coast] , killing 169.

[LINK: (2006) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2006]  – The  [LINK: (Goleta postal facility shootings) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goleta_postal_facility_shootings]  occur, killing seven people before the perpetrator took her own life. [LINK: ([24]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-24]

[LINK: (2007) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007]  –  [LINK: (Microsoft Corporation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Corporation]  releases  [LINK: (Windows Vista) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Vista] , a major release of the operating system  [LINK: (Microsoft Windows) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Windows]  and the NT based kernel. [LINK: ([25]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-25]

[LINK: (2013) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013]  –  [LINK: (Naro-1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naro-1]  becomes the first  [LINK: (carrier rocket) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Launch_vehicle]  launched by South Korea. [LINK: ([26]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-xinhua20130130-26]

[LINK: (2020) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020]  – The  [LINK: (World Health Organization) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Health_Organization]  declares the  [LINK: (COVID-19 pandemic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic]  to be a  [LINK: (Public Health Emergency of International Concern) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_Health_Emergency_of_International_Concern] . [LINK: ([27]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30#cite_note-27]


